Top 10 Kubernetes Topics You MUST Master to Crack Any DevOps Interview

1. Kubernetes Architecture (The Real Internals)
API Server, etcd, Scheduler, Controller Manager, Kubelet.
Not definitions, but the behaviour during failures.

2. Pod Lifecycle & Probes
CrashLoopBackOff patterns, liveness vs readiness vs startup.
Explain why pods restart, not just how.

3. Scheduler Logic & Node Selection
Taints, tolerations, affinities, and scoring algorithm.
If you can answer “Why did this pod land on that node?”, you’re senior.

4. ReplicaSets, Deployments & Rollout Strategy
Blue-green, canary, surge/unavailable, revision history.
Expect: “What happens inside the cluster after kubectl apply?”

5. Networking Deep Dive
CNI vs kube-proxy, DNS, MTU, packet drops, node-to-node routing.
Most rejections happen here.

6. Services & Ingress
ClusterIP, NodePort, LoadBalancer, and Ingress controllers.
Be able to trace traffic:
LB → Ingress → Service → Pod → App.

7. Resource Requests, Limits & Throttling
CPU throttling, memory eviction, QoS classes, and noisy neighbour issues.
This is where real interviews get messy.

8. ConfigMaps, Secrets & Environment Management
Update propagation, immutability, mounted secrets, and encryption.
Be ready for edge cases.

9. Troubleshooting & Observability
Events, logs, metrics, kubelet inspection, and CNI logs.
A senior’s value is measured by how they debug.

10. StatefulSets, PVCs & Storage Internals
Binding logic, storage class behaviour, access modes, volume expansion.
If you understand this deeply, you instantly stand out.
